  "status": "present",
  "value": "Inventory amounts are hundredths of a share (0..99 initially). Order quantity \"q\" is shares with at most two decimals; \"$d\" is dollars, converted to floor(d_cents*100/unit_price_cents) hundredths. Buy q: if inventory < q, buy the fewest whole shares (+100 each) to cover, then subtract q. Sell q: add q, then sell all whole shares so inventory < 100. Return [symbol, hundredths] for every symbol seen, sorted.",
